     "q": "Our water meets drinking water standards. Why is that not enough?",
     "a": "Those standards protect people, not membranes. Health Canada sets no guideline value for chloramine; the US EPA allows up to 4 mg/L. Polyamide reverse osmosis membranes typically tolerate < 0.1 mg/L of free chlorine."
