     "q": "How do you show the design covers seasonal changes?",
     "a": "In the design basis, month by month. We take [months of history] of utility and site data and size every bed for each parameter's worst month, before you order."
    },
    {
     "q": "Is pretreatment part of the validated system?",
     "a": "Your risk assessment sets the boundary. WHO TRS 1033 allows construction to drinking water standards up to the reverse osmosis stage. Either way, the turnover package covers pretreatment, with installation and operational qualification where in scope."
    },
    {
     "q": "How do you keep carbon beds clean?",
     "a": "By backwash and replacement, not hot water. Polyvinyl chloride (PVC) is rated to 60 °C, where it keeps 22 % of its pressure rating. We replace carbon every [carbon replacement interval, months], reset from counts at the sample points around each bed during qualification.",
     "link": "svc-service#running-cost"
